From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:43:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nb/intel/haswell/nri: Shorten the read round trip after
 training

The receive enable training plans the IO latencies around a receive
enable delay of 320 PI ticks and keeps rt_iocomp two qclks (four on
ULT) above its base, as margin for the board layout, and nothing takes
that margin back: read data waits in the I/O longer than it needs to.

The controller expects read data SC_ROUNDT_LAT qclks after the command,
and the I/O holds it for the IO latency of the rank plus rt_iocomp, so
for a given receive enable delay the moment the strobes come back is

  64 * (round trip - IO latency - rt_iocomp) + receive enable delay

and the three latencies can move together without changing it, as the
receive enable training of Sandy Bridge moves IO latency and logic delay
(compute_final_logic_delay). Registers of a ThinkPad W541 with four
dual-rank DDR3L-1600 SO-DIMMs, after mrc.bin and after this RAM init:
the same receive enable delays (within 4 ticks), the same difference
between the three latencies (19 qclks on channel 0, 20 on channel 1);
mrc.bin ends with rt_iocomp 21 and IO latencies of 4, this RAM init
with rt_iocomp 23 and IO latencies of 7 and 6: round trips of 44/45
qclks against 49, reads 3.1/2.5 ns shorter with mrc.bin.

Add a task after the late command training, behind
HASWELL_NRI_ROUND_TRIP: per channel, take one qclk at a time off
rt_iocomp down to its base, then off the IO latency of every rank, and
as much off the round trip latencies, while the write and read test of
the 1D margin training passes on every rank; give one qclk back as a
guard band, test again, and go back to the trained values if that
fails. The receive enable delays do not change. The values go into the
training cache with the others, so fast boots and S3 resume keep them.
When the memory test after training fails and the training is redone,
the second run leaves the round trip as trained.

TEST=On a ThinkPad W541 (i7-4810MQ, four 8 GiB DDR3L-1600 dual-rank
SO-DIMMs): an IO latency of 3 passed the test on both channels and 2
failed; with the guard band the round trips end at 44 and 45 qclks,
with IO latencies of 4 and rt_iocomp 21, the values of mrc.bin on this
machine, and the memory test after training passed. A pointer chase
over 512 MiB from Linux: 91.3 ns per read, 90.8 ns with mrc.bin
(medians of 9 runs; minimums 90.3 and 90.7 ns).

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig         |  12 +
 .../intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk  |   1 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_main.c     |   3 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/raminit_native.h   |   2 +
 .../haswell/native_raminit/train_round_trip.c | 243 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 261 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/train_round_trip.c

diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
index b426d2d35a..4e71e49ec3 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/Kconfig
@@ -28,6 +28,18 @@ config HASWELL_NRI_MEMORY_TEST
 	  that leaves a miscompare is redone once, then the boot stops. A
 	  few seconds per cold boot; fast boots and S3 resume skip it.
 
+config HASWELL_NRI_ROUND_TRIP
+	bool "Shorten the read round trip after training"
+	depends on USE_NATIVE_RAMINIT
+	help
+	  After the command training, take off the IO latencies and the
+	  round trip latency of each channel the qclks that the receive
+	  enable training keeps as margin, one at a time while a write and
+	  read test passes on every rank, and give one back as a guard band:
+	  reads return up to a few ns sooner. Best with
+	  HASWELL_NRI_MEMORY_TEST, which trains again without this when the
+	  memory test fails.
+
 config HASWELL_VBOOT_IN_BOOTBLOCK
 	depends on VBOOT
 	bool "Start verstage in bootblock"
diff --git a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk
index e525b72814..66c6f7c65a 100644
--- a/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk
+++ b/src/northbridge/intel/haswell/native_raminit/Makefile.mk
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@ romstage-y += train_late_command.c
 romstage-y += train_jedec_write_leveling.c
 romstage-y += train_read_mpr.c
 romstage-y += train_receive_enable.c
+romstage-y += train_round_trip.c
 romstage-y += train_sense_amp_offset.c
 
 romstage-$(CONFIG_DEBUG_RAM_SETUP) += info_dumps.c
